new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ops/vps/ru/DRAIN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# C2: wait for matches before an RU update or rollback
+
+This procedure belongs to the reviewed host kit. Actual RU execution still needs
+owner approval and a configured current backup/PITR kit. Never use production or
+dev aliases in place of the dedicated RU target.
+
+`ship --drain` pauses new match allocation, preserves queued parties and FIFO age,
+and waits for all current matches to finish. The running lobby must publish a
+fresh capacity report acknowledging this exact maintenance operation. Both
+occupied slots and real worker processes must reach zero before backup,
+migration, service stop or release switch. The default wait is2800 seconds;
+`--drain-timeout` accepts30..3600. Timeout leaves the previous services/matches
+running and admission paused; it never kills a match to finish an update.
+
+```sh
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py ship --package <reviewed-RU-server-bundle> --drain
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py ship --package <reviewed-RU-server-bundle> --drain --check
+# Only after the separate owner-approved host rollout:
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py ship --package <reviewed-RU-server-bundle> --drain --apply
+```
+
+The first command is a local dry run. `--check` only reads the remote preflight;
+it does not create a marker or stop services. The tool stages and verifies the
+package before opening a new maintenance operation. An existing marker is never
+borrowed or replaced, including when the lobby is stopped.
+
+After migration/restart the new release must answer its normal health checks and
+publish a newer, empty capacity acknowledgement for the same operation, with no
+worker processes. Only then does the tool remove its own maintenance marker.
+A startup/health failure attempts the existing binary/unit rollback and keeps
+admission paused. A backup/migration failure leaves the previous release in
+place and keeps the marker. No automatic database rollback is performed.
+
+A server rollback supports the same wait, without running migrations or backups:
+
+```sh
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py rollback --kind server --release <staged-release> --drain --check
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py rollback --kind server --release <staged-release> --drain --apply
+```
+
+The older binary must support the already installed schema. `--drain` is refused
+for a portal rollback. Without `--drain`, existing live-worker refusal remains.
+
+## Recover a held or uncertain operation
+
+Use the dedicated read-only view first:
+
+```sh
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py drain --action status --check
+```
+
+Inspect its exact operation ID, marker, fresh capacity report and workers,
+release history, backup result and service health. `DEPLOYED_DRAIN_HELD` returns
+nonzero and means the marker still blocks admission. A late filesystem error can
+occur after marker removal; then `DEPLOYED_RESUME_UNCONFIRMED` returns nonzero and
+records the observed marker state instead of claiming admission is held. Verify
+the real lobby/queue state; do not blindly retry a deployment or remove files.
+
+Once the selected release and services are verified healthy, the separately
+authorized operator can cancel only the exact still-active owned operation:
+
+```sh
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py drain --action cancel --operation-id <32-lowercase-hex> --check
+python3 ops/vps/ru/ru_host.py drain --action cancel --operation-id <32-lowercase-hex> --apply
+```
+
+The check form only inspects. A missing, changed, malformed, extra-entry or
+otherwise unowned marker is never recursively removed. Normal runtime resumes
+queued matchmaking after observing cancellation and requires a new unanimous
+15-second ready check. Manual maintenance is preserved by an unrelated rollback.
+
+The local controller tests use temporary files and simulated operating-system
+commands. They do not certify systemd, a real RU migration, storage, network or
+host capacity. Separate signed runtime proofs cover live-match progress,
+queue/party preservation, lobby restart/adoption and Resume. Final RU acceptance
+must exercise both the operator tool and actual services on the selected host.
